{
  "id": "Compound::DB08795 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Azidocillin is likely to interact with Slc15a2 through a shared pathway involving Slc15a1, which participates in proton-dependent peptide transport. The evidence suggests that Azidocillin binds to Slc15a1, which is involved in transporting peptides in a proton-dependent manner, and this activity is also recognized by Slc15a2. This implies that Azidocillin may influence Slc15a2 through a mechanism involving the regulation of proton-dependent peptide transport. The consistent binding of Azidocillin to Slc15a1 and its participation in transport activities that are also recognized by Slc15a2 suggests a potential functional link between the two entities. The overlapping roles of Slc15a1 in different transport processes support the idea that Azidocillin may modulate Slc15a2 through a mechanism involving the regulation of these transport activities.",
